## Your work package: WP-7 — Documentation: README, API reference, operations runbook, changelog
{
 "id": "WP-7",
 "title": "Documentation: README, API reference, operations runbook, changelog",
 "description": "Docs must match this design's contract exactly (names, paths, statuses, log messages, SQL). Remove every 'no authentication' statement.\n\n1) README.md:\n- Replace the security notice with API-key auth: X-API-Key on /api/links*, 401 {\"detail\": \"Invalid or missing API key\"}, fails closed when API_KEY is unset, minimum 16 characters; redirects and probes are public.\n- Configuration table lists ALL env vars: DATABASE_URL, BASE_URL, SHORT_CODE_LENGTH, CODE_MAX_ATTEMPTS, IP_HASH_SALT, LOG_LEVEL, API_KEY, SQLITE_BUSY_TIMEOUT_MS, DB_POOL_SIZE, DB_MAX_OVERFLOW, DB_POOL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS, with defaults and ranges from the design config.\n- Features: link expiry (expires_at, PATCH), hourly stats, HEAD probes, WAL.\n- API overview table adds PATCH /api/links/{code}, GET /api/links/{code}/stats/hourly, HEAD /healthz and HEAD /readyz, and adds 401 to every /api/links row and 410 'Link has expired' to the redirect.\n- Examples include X-API-Key and expires_at.\n- Project layout adds app/core/schema.py.\n\n2) docs/API.md:\n- Authentication section.\n- HEAD /healthz and HEAD /readyz.\n- expires_at in the POST request/response and in GET detail (plus is_expired): UTC normalisation, naive treated as UTC, must be in the future, 'Z' output, idempotency semantics (409 when expires_at differs; old keys replay).\n- PATCH /api/links/{code} with body, null clearing, 200/401/404/422, and that it never reactivates.\n- GET /api/links/{code}/stats/hourly: start/end, half-open, flooring and rounding up, both-or-neither, default 25 hours, 744-hour cap, zero-filled response, a full JSON example, and URL-encoding '+' as %2B.\n- Redirect 410 'Link has expired' vs 'Link has been deactivated' (precedence), Cache-Control no-store on 404/410.\n- Error table includes 401 and 422.\n\n3) docs/OPERATIONS.md:\n- Startup steps: create_all, then the automatic schema upgrade adding links.expires_at, with log messages 'schema upgrade: links.expires_at added' / 'already present' / 'schema upgrade failed: could not add links.expires_at' (startup aborts). Back up before deploying. Manual SQL: SQLite/MySQL 'ALTER TABLE links ADD COLUMN expires_at DATETIME;', PostgreSQL 'ALTER TABLE links ADD COLUMN expires_at TIMESTAMP WITHOUT TIME ZONE;'.\n- The startup 'database tuning ...' line and its fields.\n- HEAD probes and monitor config.\n- Log events table updated: WARNING 'failed to record click for link_id=<id> (<ExceptionClass>)'.\n- WAL: -wal/-shm files, local writable directory, no network filesystems, backups via sqlite3 .backup or copying all three files while stopped.\n- Corrected locking runbook: readers are not blocked under WAL; click writes wait up to SQLITE_BUSY_TIMEOUT_MS and are then dropped with a WARNING while the redirect still returns 307; creates may return 503 after the timeout; if the lookup itself fails, the redirect returns 503.\n- Pool sizing.\n- Data model table adds expires_at.\n- MySQL collation note with 'ALTER TABLE links MODIFY code VARCHAR(32) CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_bin NOT NULL;'.\n- Security notes corrected (API key).\n- New section '## Campaign deployment':\n  - Targets ~50 RPS, redirect p95 < 100 ms, best effort, one instance.\n  - Topology: one instance, one uvicorn worker (--workers 1 --no-access-log), SQLite WAL on local disk.\n  - Recommended SQLITE_BUSY_TIMEOUT_MS=1000, DB_POOL_SIZE=5, DB_MAX_OVERFLOW=10, DB_POOL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=30.\n  - Setting expires_at to the confirmed campaign end (example 2025-12-31T23:59:00Z; confirm the year and instant with marketing) on new links (POST) and existing links (a PATCH loop over the code list), verified with GET /api/links/{code} (expires_at, is_expired).\n  - Pulling hourly clicks per TV slot, with UTC conversion examples including a half-hour-offset zone and %2B encoding.\n  - Pre-launch checklist: the startup tuning and schema log lines; HEAD /healthz and HEAD /readyz return 200 and the monitor is configured; backup taken; expiry verified on every campaign link; hourly query returns data for a test link; ~50 RPS smoke load with p95 < 100 ms.\n  - Restart and recovery steps.\n- New section '## Scaling beyond the campaign profile': multiple workers, multiple replicas or more than ~50 RPS require PostgreSQL. Steps: add and pin a driver, set DATABASE_URL, create the schema on a fresh DB by starting the app, copy the data, size the pool per worker (workers \u00d7 (DB_POOL_SIZE + DB_MAX_OVERFLOW) \u2264 max_connections). No driver ships in this release.\n\n4) CHANGELOG.md: [Unreleased] with Added / Changed / Fixed / Security entries covering:\n- API-key authentication (and correcting the 1.0.0 security notes)\n- HEAD probes\n- WAL, busy timeout and pool settings\n- SQL stats aggregation\n- links.expires_at with the automatic startup upgrade\n- the expired 410\n- PATCH expiry\n- the hourly stats endpoint\n- the MySQL collation note",
 "files": [
  "README.md",
  "docs/API.md",
  "docs/OPERATIONS.md",
  "CHANGELOG.md"
 ],
 "depends_on": [
  "WP-1",
  "WP-3"
 ],
 "fr_ids": [
  "FR-20",
  "FR-19"
 ],
 "risk": "low"
}

