   "docs/OPERATIONS.md documents:\n- WAL and its -wal/-shm files\n- backups (sqlite3 .backup, or copying all three files while the service is stopped)\n- that WAL needs a local, writable directory and no network filesystem\n- the corrected locking runbook\n- pool sizing\n- the automatic startup schema upgrade that adds links.expires_at, with the advice to back up before deploying and the equivalent manual SQL",
   "docs/OPERATIONS.md has a 'Campaign deployment' section. It covers:\n- the targets: ~50 RPS, redirect p95 < 100 ms, best effort, one instance\n- the topology: one instance, one uvicorn worker, SQLite with WAL on local disk\n- recommended SQLITE_BUSY_TIMEOUT_MS and pool values\n- how to set expires_at to the confirmed campaign end on new links (POST) and on existing campaign links (PATCH), and how to verify it with GET /api/links/{code}\n- how to pull hourly clicks for each TV ad slot, with UTC conversion guidance for local broadcast times\n- a pre-launch checklist: startup tuning and schema log lines, HEAD /readyz monitor, backup taken, expiry verified on every campaign link\n- restart and recovery steps",
