## Approved design (shared by all packages)
{
 "overview": "Brownfield change to the layered FastAPI/SQLAlchemy URL shortener to get it ready for the campaign (Q-1: about 50 RPS, redirect p95 < 100 ms, one instance; Q-2: hardened SQLite, no new driver). The change is additive and low-risk.\n\n(1) SQLite hardening and pool settings in app/core/db.py:\n- A connect listener runs the literal PRAGMAs journal_mode=WAL and synchronous=NORMAL, only for file-based SQLite.\n- The busy timeout is set through the sqlite3 connect_args 'timeout'.\n- QueuePool size, overflow and timeout come from four new validated settings.\n- In-memory SQLite gets no pool kwargs and no WAL.\n\n(2) Startup schema upgrade in a new app/core/schema.py. It runs in the lifespan after create_all, is idempotent, and adds the only schema change: the nullable links.expires_at column (literal ALTER TABLE). If the upgrade fails, startup fails.\n\n(3) Startup log lines. One structured line reports the effective DB tuning and one reports the schema-upgrade outcome. Neither contains the URL or any secrets.\n\n(4) Redirect hot path:\n- One narrow SELECT (id, url, is_active, expires_at) into a RedirectTarget dataclass.\n- One shared private service helper checks deactivation first, then expiry (now >= expires_at, using an injectable clock).\n- The read transaction ends before the click INSERT.\n- The click is still recorded synchronously and best-effort; a failure logs one WARNING without the IP.\n- Errors on the redirect path (404/410) carry Cache-Control: no-store.\n- Expired links return 410 {\"detail\": \"Link has expired\"}.\n\n(5) Expiry API:\n- POST /api/links accepts an optional expires_at; the idempotency hash covers it only when it is present, so old keys still replay.\n- New PATCH /api/links/{code} sets or clears expires_at.\n- Create and detail responses return expires_at; detail also returns is_expired.\n\n(6) Analytics:\n- Daily stats are aggregated in SQL with GROUP BY and dialect-guarded day expressions. The response contract is unchanged.\n- New GET /api/links/{code}/stats/hourly returns zero-filled UTC-hour buckets over [start, end), capped at 744 hours, aggregated in SQL with dialect-guarded hour expressions that use no bound parameters.\n\n(7) Probes: explicit HEAD routes for /healthz and /readyz, outside the OpenAPI schema, so HEAD probes no longer fall through to the catch-all.\n\n(8) MySQL: binary collation on links.code through a String.with_variant that applies only to mysql/mariadb.\n\n(9) Docs: README, API, OPERATIONS (WAL, backups, locking, the upgrade, a campaign runbook and the PostgreSQL scaling path) and CHANGELOG are corrected.\n\nAll other contracts are unchanged: the 307 with exact Location and no-store, the 410 on deactivation, the error JSON, the auth on /api/links*, the daily stats schema, and the layering rules. requirements.txt is unchanged.",
