   "description": "No new requirements.txt entries. Core must not import app.api, app.services or app.repositories. Never use the identifier 'cache' or 'lru_cache'. text()/exec_driver_sql may only receive literal strings.\n\n1) app/core/config.py: add fields to Settings and update the module docstring to list the new env names.\n- sqlite_busy_timeout_ms: int = Field(5000, ge=0, le=60000)\n- db_pool_size: int = Field(5, ge=1)\n- db_max_overflow: int = Field(10, ge=0)\n- db_pool_timeout_seconds: float = Field(30.0, gt=0, le=300)\nKeep all existing fields, defaults and validators unchanged.\n\n2) app/core/db.py:\n- Add `def is_memory_sqlite(url: URL) -> bool`: true when url.get_backend_name() == 'sqlite' and (url.database in (None, '', ':memory:') or url.database.startswith('file::memory:') or url.query.get('mode') == 'memory').\n- Change the signature to `create_db_engine(database_url: str, *, pool_size: int = 5, max_overflow: int = 10, pool_timeout: float = 30.0, sqlite_busy_timeout_ms: int = 5000) -> Engine`. Use make_url(database_url) and call `create_engine` through the module-level imported name (tests monkeypatch app.core.db.create_engine).\n  (a) In-memory SQLite: create_engine(database_url, connect_args={'check_same_thread': False}). No pool kwargs, no listener.\n  (b) File SQLite: create_engine(database_url, poolclass=QueuePool, pool_size=pool_size, max_overflow=max_overflow, pool_timeout=pool_timeout, connect_args={'check_same_thread': False, 'timeout': (sqlite_busy_timeout_ms + 0.5) / 1000.0}). Comment that the +0.5 makes pysqlite's int(timeout*1000) truncation exact. Then register `@event.listens_for(engine, 'connect')` def _sqlite_on_connect(dbapi_connection, _record): cursor = dbapi_connection.cursor(); try: cursor.execute('PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL'); cursor.execute('PRAGMA synchronous=NORMAL'); finally: cursor.close(). Use only literal strings and do not swallow errors. Do NOT enable foreign_keys.\n  (c) Otherwise: create_engine(database_url, pool_pre_ping=True, pool_size=..., max_overflow=..., pool_timeout=...).\n- Add `def describe_engine(engine: Engine) -> dict[str, object]`, returning {'dialect': engine.dialect.name, 'pool_class': type(engine.pool).__name__, 'pool_size': ..., 'max_overflow': ..., 'pool_timeout': ...}.\n  - For a QueuePool, use pool.size(), pool._max_overflow and pool.timeout(). Otherwise all three are None.\n  - For dialect 'sqlite', also open `with engine.connect() as conn:` and read journal_mode = conn.exec_driver_sql('PRAGMA journal_mode').scalar(), synchronous = ...('PRAGMA synchronous').scalar() and busy_timeout_ms = ...('PRAGMA busy_timeout').scalar().\n  - Never include the URL.\n- Add `def log_engine_tuning(engine: Engine) -> dict[str, object]`: info = describe_engine(engine); then logging.getLogger('app.db').info('database tuning ' + ' '.join(f'{k}={v}' for k, v in info.items()), extra=info); return info. Building the log message with formatting is fine because it is not SQL.\n- create_session_factory and get_db are unchanged.\n\n3) NEW app/core/schema.py:\n- `logger = logging.getLogger('app.db')`.\n- `def ensure_links_expires_at(engine: Engine) -> bool` (True if the column was added):\n  - with engine.connect() as conn: columns = {c['name'] for c in inspect(conn).get_columns('links')}.\n  - If 'expires_at' is in columns: logger.info('schema upgrade: links.expires_at already present', extra={'schema_upgrade': 'already_present'}) and return False.\n  - Otherwise, with engine.begin() as conn: if engine.dialect.name == 'postgresql': conn.exec_driver_sql('ALTER TABLE links ADD COLUMN expires_at TIMESTAMP WITHOUT TIME ZONE'); else: conn.exec_driver_sql('ALTER TABLE links ADD COLUMN expires_at DATETIME').\n  - Then logger.info('schema upgrade: links.expires_at added', extra={'schema_upgrade': 'added'}) and return True.\n  - Wrap the whole body in try/except Exception: logger.exception('schema upgrade failed: could not add links.expires_at'); raise.\n\n4) app/core/errors.py:\n- Add `LINK_EXPIRED_DETAIL = 'Link has expired'`.\n- Add `class InvalidInputError(AppError): status_code = 422; default_detail = 'Invalid input'`.\n- Nothing else changes (the existing handlers already map AppError).\n\n5) app/core/logging.py: extend _EXTRA_FIELDS to ('method', 'path', 'status', 'duration_ms', 'dialect', 'pool_class', 'pool_size', 'max_overflow', 'pool_timeout', 'journal_mode', 'synchronous', 'busy_timeout_ms', 'schema_upgrade'). No other change.\n\n6) app/models/base.py: add `def to_naive_utc(value: datetime) -> datetime`. It returns the value unchanged if naive (tzinfo None or utcoffset None), else value.astimezone(UTC).replace(tzinfo=None). It may raise OverflowError, which callers handle.\n\n7) app/models/__init__.py: export to_naive_utc in imports and __all__.\n\n8) app/models/link.py:\n- Add `expires_at: Mapped[datetime | None] = mapped_column(DateTime, nullable=True)` after deactivated_at, with a docstring note: naive UTC, NULL = never expires.\n- Change code to `mapped_column(String(32).with_variant(String(32, collation='utf8mb4_bin'), 'mysql', 'mariadb'), nullable=False)`.\n- Use only sqlalchemy core types; no sqlalchemy.dialects import.",
